cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "kvu: a generator and measurement bench for lattice gauge theory (SU(2) Wilson action, single-source HIP/CUDA kernels, FP64 CPU reference)"
abstract: >-
  kvu is a Rust command-line tool for lattice gauge theory, centred on four-dimensional SU(2) Yang-Mills theory with
  the Wilson action. One GPU kernel source serves two backends, HIP (AMD) and CUDA (NVIDIA), compiled at run time, next
  to a double-precision CPU reference. It provides a heat-bath and overrelaxation generator with counter-based Philox
  random numbers (FP64 reference, bit-identical to su2-heatbath-gpu with the compat-prod options, and a fast FP32 mode),
  Dirichlet boxes, a conditional heat bath, Wilson and Polyakov loops, gradient flow and topology, Balaban and Swendsen
  block-spin maps, effective-coupling estimators, verifiable compressed archives of configurations, couplings of a
  truncated effective action (plaquette, rectangle, chair, twist) by pseudo-likelihood and Schwinger-Dyson equations,
  block-face flux statistics, 't Hooft twisted boundary conditions, provenance manifests for every run and bit-exact
  regeneration. It is an instrument: it contains and claims no physics result.
